```
Title: Microsoft Office Application Loading Task Scheduler DLL
Author: Saksham Bhattarai, Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
Date: 2026-11-04
Level: medium
Description: Detects a Microsoft Office application loading taskschd.dll, which exposes COM interfaces for managing Windows Scheduled Tasks.
 This load is an early precursor to scheduled task creation or modification and has been frequently observed in macro-enabled
 malicious documents attempting to establish persistence.
MITRE Tactic: Persistence
Tags: attack.persistence, attack.privilege-escalation, attack.t1053.005, attack.execution, attack.t1204.002
Reference: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_office_taskschd_dll_load.yml
 False Positives:
   - Legitimate add-ins or automation scripts that use Office applications to manage scheduled tasks (rare in most environments)
```
ImageLoaded="*\\taskschd.dll" OR OriginalFileName="taskschd.dll" Image IN ("*\\eqnedt32.exe", "*\\excel.exe", "*\\fltldr.exe", "*\\graph.exe", "*\\msaccess.exe", "*\\mspub.exe", "*\\onenote.exe", "*\\onenoteim.exe", "*\\onenotem.exe", "*\\outlook.exe", "*\\powerpnt.exe", "*\\visio.exe", "*\\winproj.exe", "*\\winword.exe")